      "side": 1,
      "message": "Although carried over from the pre-existing code, casting `ls + ...` to `(int32_t *)` here (and on lines 73, 75, 77, 103, 104, and 129) is undefined behavior because callers pass `levels` backed by an unaligned `uint8_t levels_buf[TX_PAD_2D]` (`-fsanitize\u003dundefined` flags misaligned `int32_t` stores when `levels` is not 4-byte aligned, `-Wcast-align` warns, and writing `int32_t` into a `uint8_t[]` violates strict aliasing). Since `aom_dsp/x86/synonyms.h` is already included and `zero` is defined on line 27, replacing `*(int32_t *)(ls + ...) \u003d 0` with `xx_storel_32(ls + ..., zero)` (or `memset(ls + ..., 0, 4)`) emits the exact same `movl $0, disp(%reg)` instruction without UB.",
